Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/lib/opt.c
Line: 1217
Function: opt_help
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: In the width calculation loop, the code calls strlen(o->name) without excluding sentinel control entries (OPT_HELP_STR, OPT_SECTION_STR, OPT_PARAM_STR), which are non-string pointer constants. When such an entry is encountered, strlen dereferences an invalid pointer, causing an out-of-bounds read/crash. Only OPT_MORE_STR is skipped, so passing a list containing other sentinels triggers this bug.

